Z||000002||batboy||07-02-99||01:16 PM||||Your Fiero isn't dead, it just needs some major surgery. My 87 with a 2.5 has one cylinder with almost no compression and it's using oil real bad, but it seems to still run good. Not bad for a 3 cylinder I guess. Those 2.5's just don't know when to quit until they're totally worn out. I'm trying to get my V8 Fiero all fixed up, so I can give the other one a heart transplant. Hate to have them both down at the same time and to be completely Fieroless.
Z||000003||lowCG||07-02-99||01:23 PM||||Good time to clean the subframe and replace the old hoses,heck,even if they stopped selling gas,the space where the tank is will fit several batteries,never give up.
Z||000004||Racer 1||07-02-99||03:14 PM||||My 2.5 pushes iol into the aircleaner also.SO I stuck on a remote oil breather bottle to cure the problem.I think the mechanics were lieing to you.Because you would be smoking blue smoke out the tailpipe if pistons and rings were worn?
Z||000005||theogre||07-02-99||09:44 PM||||blowing oil out the breather is caused by only one thing, crank case pressurization.<p>It would seem that a car doing this would be smoking like hell, but I can tell you for sure that's not always the case. It depends on exactly how the rings are failing. In this case it's likely the top ring only. That leaves the other 2 to control oil, but they can't take the pressure so you get allot of blow by and oil out the breather. Anyone with this problem needs a compression test done.
Z||000006||batboy||07-02-99||11:18 PM||||If your catalytic convertor is working properly, you won't see the blue smoke like the older oil burning cars used to spew out when they were wore out. Ogre's right, do a compression check, that will tell the story. In rare cases, a faulty or the wrong PVC valve might siphon oil up into the air cleaner. Usually though, it's blow-by that's doing it and that means something is worn out, most likely the rings.
Z||000007||overlord||07-06-99||12:06 PM||||i actually repalced the pcv valve and filter...hoping that was the problm but didnt fix it.<p>then i did compression test..<br>#1..50psi<br>#2..100<br>#3..65<br>#4..70<br>and then couple days later 3 cylinders gave up.<p>anyways..she is in the shop hnow gettin a new enigine in..(i miss her already..-)  )
